# vvaharness/remediation_agent/provenance.py

Read side of a trust boundary: which on-disk finding cases this machine's Stage 10 actually produced. `security-remediation/` lives inside the untrusted scanned repository; the checkpoint state store lives outside it, so only a case that matches a stored remediation row by BOTH finding id and artifact folder counts as this run's own.

Source: `vvaharness/remediation_agent/provenance.py` (lines 1-57)
Executor: code
Called from: `vvaharness/validation/cli/_run.py` (Stage 11 case discovery); not called inside remediation_agent

// src: vvaharness/remediation_agent/provenance.py:37-57
fn owned_cases(run_id):executor=code {
  owned = {}
  for each step in store.steps_with_prefix(run_id, REMEDIATE_PREFIX) {   // external: orchestrator/store.py
    record = checkpoints.load_ckpt(_, run_id, step)
    if (record is not a dict) continue
    if (!record.finding_id || !record.artifact_dir) continue   // rows written by runner.remediate_one and interactive._remediate_one carry both
    try add (record.finding_id, resolved record.artifact_dir) to owned;
    catch OSError => continue
  }
  return owned
  // Matching both values stops a planted case that reuses a real case id under another slug folder, or a real slug with another id
}
